    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for the natural logarithm. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradLog" kindref="compound">GradLog</ref> class represents the natural logarithm function in the computational graph, computing gradients for the elementwise logarithm operation. For the operation <formula id="43">$C = \ln(A)$</formula> where <formula id="12">$A$</formula> is a tensor, the gradient computation follows from the derivative of the logarithm:   <formula id="44">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{1}{A}
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="8">$\frac{\partial L}{\partial
C}$</formula> is multiplied elementwise with the reciprocal of the input according to the chain rule:    <formula id="45">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \oslash A
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves the input tensor from the forward pass as it is required to compute the gradient using the formula <formula id="46">$1/A$</formula> during the backward pass.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradExponential" kindref="compound">GradExponential</ref> for the gradient function for the natural exponential function. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
